6","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc28R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.3847\/2041-8213\/ab7eba","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc29R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/5.0101006","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc30R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.3847\/1538-4357\/ad05b8","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc31R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/0067-0049\/182\/1\/310","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc32R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.3628639","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc33R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.5022528","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc34R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022377821000489","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc35R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/mnras\/stad2231","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc36R1","unstructured":"These equations are the isothermal limit of the kinetic reduced electron heating model, a rigorous analytical framework derived from gyrokinetics under the condition of low electron plasma beta (\u03b2e\u223cme\/mi, where \u03b2e is the ratio of the electron to the magnetic pressure, and me and mi are the electron and proton masses) [32]. See Supplemental Material [37] for more details and results in the nonisothermal limit.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc37R1","unstructured":"See Supplemental Material at http:\/\/link.aps.org\/supplemental\/10.1103\/PhysRevLett.134.155201, which includes Ref.\u00a0[38,39], for an electron-only reconnection model at \u03b2\u223c1 and additional details of the simulations. These include the characteristics of reconnecting current sheets, inverse magnetic energy transfer under nonisothermal conditions, energy-transfer diagrams, and other supporting information.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc38R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.2220927120","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc39R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0065-2156(08)70100-5","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc40R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0370-1573(01)00066-7","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc41R1","unstructured":"We use &lt; instead of \u226a in order not to interfere with the ordering under which Eqs.\u00a0(1)\u2013(3) are derived (namely, \u03b2\u223cme\/mi so that \u03c1i\u223cde, see Ref.\u00a0[32]). We note that \u03b2 does not have to be numerically close to me\/mi; all that is formally required is for \u03c1i\/de not to be so large as to interfere with the asymptotic expansion parameters. Empirically, it is known that Eqs.\u00a0(1)\u2013(3) remain valid at least up to \u03b2\u223c0.1 (see Ref.\u00a0[42]). In practice, a maximum ratio of \u03c1i\/de\u224820 is acceptable if adopting the real proton-electron mass ratio.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc42R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.3847\/1538-4357\/aa894d","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc43R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/1999JA900449","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc44R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022377817000666","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc45R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.118.085101","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc46R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.128.025002","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc47R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022377818000041","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc49R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.871925","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc50R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1134\/1.952886","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc51R1","unstructured":"This initial configuration is approximately an equilibrium but it is unstable to coalescence instability [52]. We choose this configuration instead of the typical Harris sheet [53] for consistency with the study of the inverse magnetic energy transfer problem discussed below. However, we do not expect the results to be sensitive to the specific configuration chosen.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc52R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.861709","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc53R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BF02733547","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc54R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1086\/444490","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc55R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.2836623","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc56R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1063\/1.2901194","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc57R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/0004-637X\/750\/2\/129","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc58R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/2017JA024004","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc59R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.111.025002","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc60R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S002237781400107X","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc61R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0022377819000941","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc62R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/95GL03183","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc63R1","unstructured":"The fit is slightly worse for k\u22a5,max than for E due to the discrete nature of this diagnostic and the limited change in the value of k\u22a5,max, given the constrained size of the simulation domain.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc64R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/0004-637X\/701\/1\/236","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc65R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2019GL083301","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc66R1","unstructured":"Before the system settles into a natural state of decaying turbulence described by our theory, it undergoes a transient stage characterized by the development of strong turbulence. An essential indicator of strong turbulence is the establishment of critical balance, where flux tubes initially confined to box length break in the z direction. This reduction in the parallel coherence length l is captured by the first two data points in Fig.\u00a02.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc67R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/2041-8205\/758\/2\/L44","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc68R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/2016GL068747","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc69R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2019GL083301","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc70R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.2119831119","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevLett.134.155201Cc71R1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"12","DOI":"10.3847\/1538-4357\/ad0b0f","type":"journal-article","volume":"960","author":"M. Zhou","year":"2023","journal-title":"Astrophys. J.","ISSN":"https:\/\/id.crossref.org\/issn\/0004-637X","issn-type":"print"}],"container-title":["Physical Review Letters"],"original-title":[],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/link.aps.org\/accepted\/10.1103\/PhysRevLett.134.155201","content-type":"ap